ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":91,"prev":93,"next":96,"titles":99,"firmware":27},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":28,"procedures":48,"parameters":49,"related":75,"body":77,"sources":78,"official_url":32,"controls":86},"instrument.lfo-element","Element LFO (gyroscope, microphone, envelope)",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"element","gyro","gyroscope","tilt","motion control","microphone modulation","mic lfo","instrument",42,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/lfo-element.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[12],[18],"M4","The element LFO turns the unit's own sensors into a modulation source — tilt (gyroscope), the built-in microphone, the amp envelope, or all three summed.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[24,25],"1.0.50","1.1.0","1.1.15","1.1.33",[29,35,39,43],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"what","Element takes its modulation from the OP-XY itself rather than from an oscillator.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#lfo",null,"official",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"gyro-depth","OS 1.0.50 raised the maximum depth of gyroscope modulation.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.50",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":42,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"envelope-fix","OS 1.1.0 fixed a bug that affected element when the amp envelope was its source.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":47},"screen","Element shows its source as an icon — G for the gyroscope, a microphone, ^ for the envelope, or sum — then amount on a tick ladder, destination cards (synth wave, env, filter, amp) and a card naming the parameter, such as attack, cutoff, pitch or pan.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#24-lfo-instrument-m4-five-typ